(Japanese: '''ラプラスの海''' ''Laplace's Sea'') is an {{pkmn|animated series}}-exclusive location featured in {{aniseries|HZ}}. It is an area where similar reports of sudden mists sweeping across cargo ships have been reported in recent times, as a direct result of {{TP|Lucius|Lapras}} and her crew's pirate-like activity. [[Diana]] referred to this group of Pokémon as the "Lapras Pirates".
[[File:Lapras Pirates versus Rising Volt Tacklers.png|thumb|left|250px|The Lapras Pirates facing the [[Rising Volt Tacklers]]]]
Lapras Sea first appeared in ''[[HZ031|Song Within the Mist]]'', where a shining Lapras was seen guiding a ship lost in the mist back to safety with her song; unbeknownst to the crew, however, this was a ruse to allow Lapras's accomplices to steal their food supplies. The [[Rising Volt Tacklers]] managed to get in contact with the ship's crew before heading towards the open sea, when a mist suddenly rolled in. This time, however, Lapras's strategy failed, as [[Liko]] and [[Roy]] intercepted two of her crew members, an {{p|Ambipom}} and a {{p|Toedscruel}}, before they scrambled away on a {{p|Wailord}}. Noticing something was off, [[Friede]] came up with a plan to attract the pirates and reveal their true intentions, which was successful.

In the [[HZ032|following episode]], after figuring out Lapras's true intentions, the Rising Volt Tacklers gave chase, but the [[Brave Olivine]] was frozen by an {{m|Ice Beam}}. Liko managed to track down the pirates' hideout by following the empty food boxes drifting at sea. Lapras reunited with [[Pagogo]], {{TP|Lucius|Arboliva}}, and {{TP|Lucius|Moltres}} before deciding to aid the Rising Volt Tacklers in finding [[Laqua]]. The rest of her crew left the reef to continue their lifestyle elsewhere.
